The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.


Short description
-----------------

convection_diffusion1:

 Steady scalar convection-diffusion problem on a unit square with
 Dirichlet boundary conditions and natural boundary conditions.
 Varying alpha coefficient using a function or a vector in the nodes.
 Varying velocity coefficient using a function.

convection_diffusion2:

 Steady scalar convection-diffusion problem on a unit square with
 Dirichlet boundary conditions and natural boundary conditions.
 Varying alpha tensor coefficient using a function.
 Varying velocity coefficient using a function.

convection_diffusion3:

 Time-dependent scalar convection-diffusion problem on a unit square with
 Dirichlet boundary conditions and natural boundary conditions.
 Varying alpha coefficient using a function or a vector in the nodes.
 Varying velocity coefficient using a function.
 Second-order implicit Gear discretization. First step: Euler implicit.

convection_diffusion4:

 Time-dependent scalar convection-diffusion problem on a unit square with
 Dirichlet boundary conditions and natural boundary conditions.
 Varying alpha coefficient using a function or a vector in the nodes.
 Varying beta coefficient using a function or a vector in the nodes.
 Varying velocity coefficient using a function.
 Second-order implicit Gear discretization. First step: Euler implicit.

convection_diffusion5:

 Time-dependent scalar convection-diffusion problem on a unit square with
 Dirichlet boundary conditions and natural boundary conditions.
 Varying alpha coefficient using a function or a vector in the nodes.
 Varying beta coefficient using a function or a vector in the nodes.
 Varying velocity coefficient using a function.
 Crank-Nicolson time discretization.

convection_diffusion6:

 Time-dependent scalar convection-diffusion problem on a unit square with
 Dirichlet boundary conditions and natural boundary conditions.
 Varying alpha tensor coefficient using a function.
 Varying beta coefficient using a function or a vector in the nodes.
 Varying velocity coefficient using a function.
 Crank-Nicolson time discretization.

convection_diffusion7:

 Steady scalar convection-diffusion problem in 1D on an interval (0,L):

   u dc/dx - d/dx ( alpha * dc/dx ) = 0 on (0,L)

 with c(0)=c0 and c(L)=cL, using a spectral element method with a uniform grid.
 The standard elements are used.

convection_diffusion8:

 Steady scalar convection-diffusion problem on a unit square with Dirichlet
 and natural boundary conditions. There is a circular region in the domain,
 where on the boundary a jump in flux is applied (heat supply).
 This is basically an extension of diffusion7 to a convection-diffusion problem
 Weak embedded interface conditions are imposed at the cylindrical interface.
 XFEM is used to solve the problem.
 Constant or varying alpha coefficient using a function.
 Varying velocity coefficient using a function.
 Optional different weighting for both sides of the interface.
 Optional Nitsche's method.
 Optional Baumann-Oden method.
 Optional Lesaint-Raviart upwinding along the interface.
